<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Anglo says not told of EU Lonrho ruling.</title>
<headline>Anglo says not told of EU Lonrho ruling.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd said on Thursday it had not been informed of the European Commission's decision regarding its 28.4-percent stake in British conglomerate Lonrho Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not received any notification yet of the decision of the EU and therefore prefer not to comment,&quot; an Anglo spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She was responding to news from Brussels that European Union and industry sources expected the EU's executive arm to block Anglo's holding in Lonrho on competition grounds.</p>
<p>The EU is to decide by May 5 whether to grant regulatory approval for Anglo's acquisition of the stake.</p>
<p>Critics argue the deal effectively puts the platinum market under the control of Anglo and another South African mining house, Gencor Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
